01:20:06.439 --> 01:20:11.200
I guess we used to have, um, a representative from Huntsville Utilities

01:20:11.200 --> 01:20:15.959
come to the podium every meeting to give us a report on any issues of concern

01:20:15.959 --> 01:20:16.959
and so we're gonna start.

01:20:17.120 --> 01:20:18.120
Heading in today and Mr.

01:20:18.129 --> 01:20:22.160
Gerdes is here with us to bring us matters of concern from Huntsville Utilities.

01:20:22.299 --> 01:20:24.990
Thank you, Council President Joe Gerdes, External Affairs,

01:20:25.000 --> 01:20:26.149
Huntsville Utilities.

01:20:26.439 --> 01:20:31.649
Uh, we had this conversation internally and we had a much more routine cadence

01:20:31.649 --> 01:20:35.450
of appearing before council even when we didn't have items on the agenda

01:20:35.450 --> 01:20:37.359
just to address some of the concerns.

01:20:37.850 --> 01:20:42.729
Uh, we want the viewing public and council to know we are aware that people's

01:20:42.729 --> 01:20:44.229
bills are up.

01:20:44.770 --> 01:20:45.609
It is hot.

01:20:46.640 --> 01:20:48.399
Uh, it is unavoidable.

01:20:48.439 --> 01:20:54.240
It is weather driven, um, when you have low temperatures that don't go below

01:20:54.240 --> 01:20:59.209
where people set their thermostats, your cooling equipment is going to run

01:20:59.439 --> 01:21:03.359
a lot, and that's the biggest that and your,

01:21:03.439 --> 01:21:06.189
uh, heating appliances like water heaters and such,

01:21:06.520 --> 01:21:09.330
those are the biggest drivers of your utility bill.

01:21:09.759 --> 01:21:13.859
Uh, council has asked us over the years and we have complied with.

01:21:14.560 --> 01:21:18.390
Finding ways to communicate energy efficiency tips with our customers,

01:21:18.720 --> 01:21:23.000
that is a constant effort, uh, we have never been better armed to do that

01:21:23.000 --> 01:21:25.859
and we're doing that now via our website,

01:21:25.870 --> 01:21:30.049
via our web portal, via our mobile app we also,

01:21:30.080 --> 01:21:34.939
uh, our friends in the local media give us a lot of attention on those things,

01:21:35.359 --> 01:21:39.640
but, uh, you know, there's, there are often comments made on social media

01:21:39.640 --> 01:21:43.759
where, uh, folks worry that we've raised our rates we have not.

01:21:44.620 --> 01:21:48.720
Um, it is just the matter of hot weather.

01:21:48.870 --> 01:21:54.589
Uh, your utility bill is weather driven, and if you have concerns about

01:21:54.589 --> 01:21:56.350
your bill, please call us.

01:21:57.200 --> 01:22:02.240
Also want to remind the viewing public that we recently made our home energy

01:22:02.240 --> 01:22:03.220
audit free.

01:22:04.529 --> 01:22:08.029
So if you think something in your home is malfunctioning.

01:22:08.899 --> 01:22:12.819
You can call us and set up a time for a technician to come out and do an

01:22:12.819 --> 01:22:17.609
audit on your home and help you identify what those things are,

01:22:18.020 --> 01:22:22.100
uh, then, then the homeowner, the customer is armed with a way to react

01:22:22.100 --> 01:22:27.200
to maybe some high usage that they could avoid through some maintenance

01:22:27.200 --> 01:22:29.240
insulation, things of that nature.

01:22:29.649 --> 01:22:33.009
So just wanted to reassure everyone that we have not raised our rates,

01:22:33.020 --> 01:22:37.680
we have no plans to raise any rates in the foreseeable future.

01:22:37.939 --> 01:22:43.220
And of course when we do need to do that you will have plenty of notice.

01:22:43.540 --> 01:22:45.620
Thank you so much for the time, Council President.

01:22:45.990 --> 01:22:46.339
Thank you.

