Our rescue has provided food, veterinary care,

02:28:29.169 --> 02:28:31.650
vaccinations, transportation, collars, leashes,

02:28:31.769 --> 02:28:35.089
blankets, spay and neuter services, and even offered to accept animals into

02:28:35.089 --> 02:28:37.959
our rescue when owners could no longer care for them.

02:28:38.330 --> 02:28:41.440
Unfortunately, our offers of spay and neuter services are almost always

02:28:41.440 --> 02:28:43.620
declined, allowing the cycle to continue.

02:28:44.209 --> 02:28:47.290
What we are seeing over and over again are animals whose basic needs are

02:28:47.290 --> 02:28:50.169
not being met despite extensive assistance being offered.

02:28:51.860 --> 02:28:54.860
From January of this year to July of this year,

02:28:54.940 --> 02:28:58.299
we've invested roughly $7000 in assistance.

02:28:58.540 --> 02:29:00.980
That does not include medication, supplies,

02:29:01.139 --> 02:29:03.160
transportation, volunteer time, or food.

02:29:04.360 --> 02:29:10.309
Uh, this turns out to be an average of a minimum of $1000 a month and $12,000

02:29:10.309 --> 02:29:10.740
a year.

02:29:12.469 --> 02:29:14.429
These cases we encounter are severe.

02:29:14.589 --> 02:29:17.370
We have treated dogs suffering from pyometra requiring,

02:29:17.669 --> 02:29:22.129
uh, emergency surgery, rescue dogs with cords wrapped around their necks,

02:29:22.469 --> 02:29:25.910
responded to dog attacks, and taken in puppies that tested positive for

02:29:25.910 --> 02:29:30.030
methamphetamine exposure after being found in environments where their owners

02:29:30.030 --> 02:29:32.059
were incapacitated by drug use.

02:29:32.629 --> 02:29:34.530
These are not isolated incidents.

02:29:34.589 --> 02:29:38.549
They are reoccurring cases that consume limited nonprofit resources while

02:29:38.549 --> 02:29:39.959
animals continue to suffer.

02:29:40.580 --> 02:29:43.580
I also want to acknowledge that Huntsville Animal Services has worked with

02:29:43.580 --> 02:29:47.000
us and that we appreciate the officers responding to the calls that we make.

02:29:47.740 --> 02:29:52.169
However, our current system is not producing positive outcomes in many situations.

02:29:52.349 --> 02:29:56.639
For example, dogs are routinely left tied to the fence outside of First

02:29:56.639 --> 02:29:59.540
Stop, which is nearby us, for hours.

02:29:59.940 --> 02:30:03.200
Monday, August 3rd, 1 remained there for approximately 3 hours,

02:30:03.330 --> 02:30:04.160
3 hours.

02:30:05.440 --> 02:30:08.580
When these situations are reported this particular day,

02:30:09.240 --> 02:30:14.309
uh, at 9:30 a.m. and 12:00 p.m. by me, the response is often that the dog

02:30:14.309 --> 02:30:16.320
has an owner and therefore little can be done.

02:30:17.150 --> 02:30:19.370
That raises an important policy question.

02:30:19.910 --> 02:30:22.589
How is ownership being verified or defined?

02:30:22.910 --> 02:30:27.730
Many of these dogs have no microchip, no vet records establishing ownership,

02:30:27.790 --> 02:30:30.309
and they frequently change hands within the encampment.

02:30:30.750 --> 02:30:34.839
If an ownership cannot be objectively verified and an animal is repeatedly

02:30:34.839 --> 02:30:36.759
found in conditions that threaten its welfare,

02:30:36.879 --> 02:30:38.519
there should be a clear Barra, I'm sorry,

02:30:38.599 --> 02:30:39.559
your time is up.

02:30:40.030 --> 02:30:41.459
Your, your 3 minutes is up.

02:30:41.830 --> 02:30:45.639
Um, you have raised some really important issues that we didn't,

02:30:45.799 --> 02:30:47.780
I, I, I certainly didn't know about.

02:30:48.040 --> 02:30:49.639
Our director of animal services, Mr.

02:30:49.759 --> 02:30:50.900
Fisher, is here.

02:30:51.160 --> 02:30:54.400
If you all would like to go, um, we speak weekly,

02:30:54.549 --> 02:30:57.980
multiple times a week, so this is kind of beyond our.

02:30:58.429 --> 02:31:01.700
Um, perhaps, perhaps you could arrange a meeting with,

02:31:02.190 --> 02:31:05.480
uh, council members, individual council members at some time to,

02:31:05.620 --> 02:31:06.440
so we'd have more time.

02:31:06.559 --> 02:31:07.519
3 minutes is not of time.

02:31:07.709 --> 02:31:09.780
OK, so, so you would be open to that.

02:31:09.879 --> 02:31:10.700
Yes, absolutely.

02:31:10.879 --> 02:31:12.440
So we look forward to hearing from you.

02:31:12.559 --> 02:31:14.120
Please contact the council office.

02:31:14.769 --> 02:31:17.589
Thank you all so much for being here with us tonight and thank you for the

02:31:17.589 --> 02:31:18.379
work you do.

02:31:19.120 --> 02:31:20.690
We'll hear next from Andrew Sullens.

02:31:21.240 --> 02:31:21.919
Following Mr.

02:31:22.160 --> 02:31:24.440
Sullens, we'll hear from Angelica Condry.

02:31:26.019 --> 02:31:26.570
Good evening.

02:31:26.780 --> 02:31:30.570
My name is Andrew Sullens, and I'm a resident at 1410 Wells Avenue right

02:31:30.570 --> 02:31:31.459
here in Huntsville.

02:31:31.620 --> 02:31:32.040
Welcome.

02:31:32.459 --> 02:31:36.169
I'm here today to express my concerns with the proliferation of flock automated

02:31:36.169 --> 02:31:38.379
license plate readers throughout the city of Huntsville.

02:31:39.320 --> 02:31:43.440
These approximately 100 devices create point in time images of each passing

02:31:43.440 --> 02:31:47.440
vehicle, creating thousands of data points on tens of thousands of Puntvillians

02:31:47.440 --> 02:31:51.820
every day, accessible not only to local police but to law enforcement nationwide.

02:31:52.820 --> 02:31:57.059
Flock and HPD fact sheets defend this technology by claiming images are

02:31:57.059 --> 02:31:58.519
merely single points in time.

02:31:59.190 --> 02:32:02.469
But thousands of data points easily assemble into a mosaic of our daily

02:32:02.469 --> 02:32:03.389
travel patterns.

02:32:04.209 --> 02:32:07.389
These aggregated data points create a system prone to abuse.

02:32:07.849 --> 02:32:11.330
Nearly every day we learn of yet another misuse either nationally or right

02:32:11.330 --> 02:32:12.150
here in Alabama.

02:32:13.150 --> 02:32:17.309
A journalistic investigation has found over 50 incidents in which officers

02:32:17.309 --> 02:32:20.150
have run thousands of checks on wives, girlfriends,

02:32:20.349 --> 02:32:22.110
mistresses, and personal enemies.

02:32:22.780 --> 02:32:25.620
In just the last month, officers in Moody and Springfield,

02:32:25.700 --> 02:32:29.500
Alabama were fired or forced to resign after conducting searches on their

02:32:29.500 --> 02:32:30.339
family members.

02:32:31.360 --> 02:32:35.259
Block proponents downplay these incidents as isolated and point to the mere

02:32:35.259 --> 02:32:37.839
ability to conduct audits as sufficient oversight.

02:32:38.580 --> 02:32:41.200
They note that officers must enter a reason for each search,

02:32:41.540 --> 02:32:44.740
but neglect to mention that many log entries show vague reasons such as

02:32:44.740 --> 02:32:45.980
test or investigation.

02:32:46.809 --> 02:32:51.209
HPD says they continue to conduct system audits without any specifics or

02:32:51.209 --> 02:32:52.049
past findings.

02:32:53.009 --> 02:32:55.830
Beyond the risk of abuse, there is also a clear disparity,

02:32:56.290 --> 02:32:59.650
with more affluent wider areas of South and East Huntsville having limited

02:32:59.650 --> 02:33:04.160
cameras along 231 and 431, while working class communities of color in the

02:33:04.160 --> 02:33:07.530
North and West see dozens of devices deep into residential areas.

02:33:08.259 --> 02:33:11.530
My previous commute from Maston Lake Road took me past 3 separate block

02:33:11.530 --> 02:33:14.980
hubs, while my new commute from 5 Points takes me past a hub.

02:33:15.759 --> 02:33:19.639
If this is truly about safety, does the city not want to protect the people

02:33:19.639 --> 02:33:20.679
of Southeast Huntsville?

02:33:21.679 --> 02:33:24.169
Proponents point to solve crimes as justification.

02:33:25.139 --> 02:33:28.129
But we must ask ourselves if the ends justify the means.

02:33:28.509 --> 02:33:30.290
If Huntsville stored all of our digital data,

02:33:30.589 --> 02:33:31.889
would we solve more crimes?

02:33:32.030 --> 02:33:32.769
Absolutely.

02:33:33.389 --> 02:33:36.669
Would we, the people, happily accept the watchful eye of Big Brother for

02:33:36.669 --> 02:33:37.330
this trade-off?

02:33:37.790 --> 02:33:38.360
Unlikely.

02:33:39.110 --> 02:33:42.709
I urge the council to adopt an ordinance banning the municipal use of these

02:33:42.709 --> 02:33:45.099
types of integrated devices in city limits.

02:33:45.509 --> 02:33:48.169
If unwilling, I implore the council to, at minimum,

02:33:48.929 --> 02:33:52.990
set a clear legal requirement for quarterly audits with at least a 20% random

02:33:52.990 --> 02:33:57.230
sample size and termination of any employee found to abuse the public trust

02:33:57.230 --> 02:33:57.950
placed in them.

02:33:58.679 --> 02:34:00.500
I end with a quote from Benjamin Franklin.

02:34:01.200 --> 02:34:04.320
Those who would give up essential liberty to purchase a little temporary

02:34:04.320 --> 02:34:07.080
safety deserve neither liberty nor safety.

02:34:07.259 --> 02:34:07.799
Thank you.

02:34:08.120 --> 02:34:08.759
Thank you, sir.

02:34:09.709 --> 02:34:12.820
The next person to speak is Angelica Condri,

02:34:12.980 --> 02:34:14.790
who will be followed by Mariko Darling.

02:34:27.320 --> 02:34:28.589
Good evening council members.

02:34:28.719 --> 02:34:30.549
Huntsville 35811.

02:34:31.250 --> 02:34:34.139
Um, and your name please for the record, Angelica Condry thank you.

02:34:36.360 --> 02:34:38.879
I'm here again tonight representing Rocket City Roller Derby,

02:34:38.959 --> 02:34:42.360
but I want to focus tonight on our appropriations application because I

02:34:42.360 --> 02:34:43.679
know we're coming up on budget season.

02:34:43.759 --> 02:34:45.740
I know those numbers are on your mind right now.

02:34:46.360 --> 02:34:50.320
We have submitted an appropriations request for $50,000 and obviously whatever

02:34:50.320 --> 02:34:52.440
amount the city is able to provide would be helpful,

02:34:52.589 --> 02:34:56.099
but I want you to know what that money would actually allow us to do.

02:34:56.459 --> 02:34:59.980
We lost our long term venue which was affordable and sustainable for a for

02:34:59.980 --> 02:35:02.339
a small volunteer run nonprofit.

02:35:02.660 --> 02:35:04.959
Since losing it, we have been searching everywhere for a solution.

02:35:05.299 --> 02:35:07.580
Parks and Recreation has honestly been a support,

02:35:07.660 --> 02:35:11.139
a life support for us this season, and we're incredibly grateful for that.

02:35:11.419 --> 02:35:14.139
But basketball season is coming, and we know that we can't depend on those

02:35:14.139 --> 02:35:15.450
facilities indefinitely.

02:35:15.709 --> 02:35:18.459
The $50,000 would help us actually get established somewhere.

02:35:18.540 --> 02:35:19.740
It could help us pay the rent.

02:35:20.240 --> 02:35:23.120
And the initial rent in the facility while we get it up and running,

02:35:23.230 --> 02:35:27.009
purchasing tables, chairs, and equipment we need to put down a proper track

02:35:27.009 --> 02:35:30.009
and make the space functional for our practices and events.

02:35:30.370 --> 02:35:33.330
I'm also actively working on securing a warehouse that could potentially

02:35:33.330 --> 02:35:35.250
become that home if we're able to make that happen.

02:35:35.330 --> 02:35:38.129
This funding could help us turn an empty warehouse into a functional roller

02:35:38.129 --> 02:35:39.150
sports facility.

02:35:39.809 --> 02:35:41.809
Eventually, depending on what we are able to secure,

02:35:41.889 --> 02:35:43.790
we could even look at something like a bank track.

02:35:43.889 --> 02:35:46.730
We've talked to other skaters outside the area that have told me personally

02:35:46.730 --> 02:35:49.250
they would come to Huntsville specifically to skate if we had one.

02:35:49.809 --> 02:35:51.620
This isn't just about roller derby though.

02:35:52.040 --> 02:35:54.360
We have roller hockey, figure skating, dance skating,

02:35:54.519 --> 02:35:56.559
speed skating, and other roller sports in this city.

02:35:56.790 --> 02:35:57.700
There's a community here.

02:35:57.759 --> 02:36:00.589
It's just a community that doesn't currently have an appropriate facility.

02:36:01.000 --> 02:36:03.280
Huntsville is already losing opportunities because of that.

02:36:03.360 --> 02:36:06.759
This year we were supposed to host our annual fall mixer that is 6 teams'

02:36:06.759 --> 02:36:10.019
worth of skaters coming from across the Southeast and even the Midwest.

02:36:10.580 --> 02:36:12.570
And it's not just skaters, it's coaches, officials,

02:36:12.679 --> 02:36:14.339
families, friends, and spectators.

02:36:14.660 --> 02:36:16.660
All those people would have stayed in Huntsville hotels,

02:36:16.740 --> 02:36:18.179
eaten at Huntsville restaurants, shopped here,

02:36:18.190 --> 02:36:19.360
and spent money in our community.

02:36:19.700 --> 02:36:21.780
Instead, because we couldn't secure an appropriate facility,

02:36:21.860 --> 02:36:23.610
this event is going to Nashville this year.

02:36:24.059 --> 02:36:26.809
We also lost the opportunity to host the Yellow Hammer Roller Rumble,

02:36:26.860 --> 02:36:30.179
a 2-day statewide tournament that would have brought 4 Alabama teams along

02:36:30.179 --> 02:36:32.280
with their supporters and spectators to Huntsville.

02:36:32.820 --> 02:36:35.019
So these aren't hypothetical economic opportunities.

02:36:35.059 --> 02:36:37.259
These are 2 events that we are actually supposed to host,

02:36:37.280 --> 02:36:39.240
and we lost them because we don't have a facility.

02:36:39.790 --> 02:36:42.150
When I first came to the city, I said we weren't asking you to simply hand

02:36:42.150 --> 02:36:42.669
us a building.

02:36:42.750 --> 02:36:45.750
I still believe that, but the more I've worked with Parks and Rec and the

02:36:45.750 --> 02:36:48.190
more I've researched what's available, the more I believe Huntsville needs

02:36:48.190 --> 02:36:51.929
to start having a serious conversation about a multi-use roller sports facility.

02:36:52.469 --> 02:36:53.990
The city has invested in Stoner Park.

02:36:54.070 --> 02:36:55.349
You've invested in a skate park.

02:36:55.389 --> 02:36:57.750
You've invested in facilities for other growing sports.

02:36:58.070 --> 02:37:00.400
I think roller sports deserves that same opportunity.

02:37:00.549 --> 02:37:03.389
So tonight I'm asking you to support our appropriations request and to help

02:37:03.389 --> 02:37:05.209
us get on the path toward a sustainable home.

02:37:05.910 --> 02:37:08.019
Because we aren't asking you to build something for one team,

02:37:08.099 --> 02:37:10.660
we are asking you to invest in a community that's already here,

02:37:11.019 --> 02:37:13.940
already growing, and that it's already shown it can bring people and economic

02:37:13.940 --> 02:37:15.259
activity into Huntsville.

02:37:15.559 --> 02:37:16.790
We just need somewhere to do it.

02:37:17.019 --> 02:37:17.599
Thank you.

02:37:18.589 --> 02:37:18.610
Thank you.

02:37:20.280 --> 02:37:22.719
The next person to speak will be Mario Darling,

02:37:22.839 --> 02:37:24.679
who will be followed by Kyle Simpson.

02:37:28.559 --> 02:37:30.040
Hello, my name is Marco Darling.

02:37:30.120 --> 02:37:32.150
I live on Alpine Street in Huntsville, Alabama.

02:37:32.360 --> 02:37:32.690
Welcome.

02:37:33.150 --> 02:37:37.290
Uh, I also want to speak, um, about roller derby with Rocket City Roller

02:37:37.290 --> 02:37:37.559
derby.

02:37:38.000 --> 02:37:41.379
I want to say that we're grateful the city has continued to provide space

02:37:41.379 --> 02:37:42.740
for our practices and events.

02:37:42.839 --> 02:37:47.860
However, the lack of advanced confirmation for gym use has become a serious

02:37:47.860 --> 02:37:51.959
obstacle when we don't know whether we are going to have a venue until close

02:37:51.959 --> 02:37:52.559
to the event date.

02:37:52.639 --> 02:37:54.500
We can't effectively advertise.

02:37:55.500 --> 02:37:57.419
Sell tickets, coordinate with visiting teams,

02:37:57.459 --> 02:37:59.959
recruit volunteers, or build community support.

02:38:00.500 --> 02:38:03.500
We understand that Parks and Recreation would ultimately like us to find

02:38:03.500 --> 02:38:06.780
a permanent home of our own, and we want that too,

02:38:06.900 --> 02:38:09.610
but sustaining our own facility requires us to grow,

02:38:09.620 --> 02:38:12.919
and growth depends on successful, well promoted events.

02:38:14.059 --> 02:38:16.240
Right now we're caught in a cycle where encouraging,

02:38:16.780 --> 02:38:20.639
we're, we're encouraged to become independent of the recreation centers

02:38:20.980 --> 02:38:24.179
while the uncertainty surrounding our current space makes it harder to build

02:38:24.179 --> 02:38:26.919
that support and resources necessary to do that.

02:38:27.700 --> 02:38:30.969
This is becoming increasingly urgent as basketball season approaches,

02:38:31.950 --> 02:38:35.269
uh, when once again we'll face the possibility of losing both our practice

02:38:35.269 --> 02:38:36.429
and event space again.

02:38:37.190 --> 02:38:40.139
We want roller derby to have a lasting place in Huntsville's recreation

02:38:40.139 --> 02:38:40.490
community.

02:38:40.830 --> 02:38:43.629
We want to grow our events, bring people together,

02:38:43.709 --> 02:38:45.490
and eventually establish a home of our own,

02:38:45.750 --> 02:38:48.650
but to get there we need enough stability to build that future.

02:38:49.000 --> 02:38:49.509
Thank you.

02:38:49.750 --> 02:38:50.290
Thank you.

02:38:51.309 --> 02:38:56.669
We'll now hear from Kyle Simpson, who will be followed by KMP Carroll.

02:39:06.690 --> 02:39:07.980
My name is Kyle Simpson.

02:39:08.059 --> 02:39:11.209
I live at 187 Heritage Brook Drive in Huntsville.

02:39:11.389 --> 02:39:11.410
Thank you.

02:39:12.259 --> 02:39:14.339
Uh, good evening, Madam President, Mayor Battle,

02:39:14.459 --> 02:39:15.820
and members of the city council.

02:39:15.940 --> 02:39:18.870
I'm here to respectfully ask for your help restoring my,

02:39:18.929 --> 02:39:20.900
uh, access to the Huntsville Tennis Center,

02:39:20.980 --> 02:39:24.139
a public facility owned by the city of Huntsville.

02:39:24.820 --> 02:39:28.120
I worked at the tennis center for about 3 years while I was in high school,

02:39:28.419 --> 02:39:32.530
and in 2023 I was terminated for not completing my closing duties properly.

02:39:32.860 --> 02:39:34.719
I accepted that decision and moved on.

02:39:34.900 --> 02:39:38.040
However, I have never been accused of any misconduct,

02:39:38.099 --> 02:39:41.919
uh, beyond that, and I was never told I was banned from the facility.

02:39:42.379 --> 02:39:45.110
Or prohibited from returning as a member of the public.

02:39:45.469 --> 02:39:48.910
Shortly after my employment ended, I filed a complaint with the Alabama

02:39:48.910 --> 02:39:52.549
Department of Labor concerning my handling of alcohol while I was a minor.

02:39:52.870 --> 02:39:56.150
I did so on the advice of my parents because I believed it was the appropriate

02:39:56.150 --> 02:39:57.650
way to address my concerns.

02:39:58.059 --> 02:40:00.160
I took a break from tennis for about 3 years,

02:40:00.339 --> 02:40:03.370
and a few weeks ago, I decided to start playing again.

02:40:03.740 --> 02:40:07.160
For 4 consecutive weeks, I used the tennis center without any issues,

02:40:07.620 --> 02:40:10.000
and uh I even had my racket restrung there.

02:40:10.299 --> 02:40:13.179
Then on July 29th, when I returned to pick up my racket,

02:40:13.299 --> 02:40:14.549
I was met at the front door by the manager.

02:40:15.700 --> 02:40:20.219
Managing director Jock Simmons, who is also my former supervisor,

02:40:20.559 --> 02:40:23.200
uh, as I entered the facility, he told me verbatim,

02:40:23.360 --> 02:40:23.820
get out.

02:40:23.879 --> 02:40:27.320
You do not get to file complaints against us and play tennis here.

02:40:27.599 --> 02:40:28.519
I left immediately.

02:40:28.639 --> 02:40:30.799
I did not argue or create a disturbance.

02:40:30.860 --> 02:40:36.900
I paid all my fees, and I have not caused any issues with the facility or

02:40:36.900 --> 02:40:38.320
its management.

02:40:39.160 --> 02:40:42.969
Uh, to this day, I still have never received a written trespass notice,

02:40:43.129 --> 02:40:45.200
never been informed that I'm banned from the facility,

02:40:45.290 --> 02:40:50.190
and never been told that I violated any rule as a patron of the tennis center.

02:40:50.610 --> 02:40:52.759
I'm not asking the council to punish anyone.

02:40:52.849 --> 02:40:55.309
I'm just asking for its fairness and clarity.

02:40:55.599 --> 02:40:59.549
There is an official policy that justifies excluding me from a public recreational

02:40:59.549 --> 02:41:00.179
facility.

02:41:00.480 --> 02:41:03.200
I'd appreciate knowing what it is, and if there isn't,

02:41:03.280 --> 02:41:07.200
I respectfully ask that my access to the tennis center be restored so that

02:41:07.200 --> 02:41:11.320
I can continue playing the sport I enjoy at a public facility that serves

02:41:11.320 --> 02:41:12.019
our community.

02:41:12.480 --> 02:41:14.959
And I would just like to say I've already taken this up with Parks and Rec,

02:41:15.049 --> 02:41:17.099
and they said it's outside of their scope,

02:41:17.150 --> 02:41:21.000
and I spoke with my city representative, and he recommended I come to this

02:41:21.000 --> 02:41:22.940
forum and take it up with you guys.

02:41:23.610 --> 02:41:27.009
And I would just like to thank all of you for your time and consideration.

02:41:27.940 --> 02:41:28.610
Thank you, sir.

02:41:29.459 --> 02:41:29.740
Pardon.

02:41:31.410 --> 02:41:31.860
Thank you.

02:41:32.629 --> 02:41:37.519
